  "conformsTo": "http://mlcommons.org/croissant/1.0",
  "name": "TRACE",
  "description": "TRACE is a 10,000-dialogue benchmark for conversational tourism recommendation that jointly tests three competencies: (1) recommendation accuracy, (2) review-grounded citation evidence, and (3) rejection recovery. Each multi-turn dialogue between a persona-driven user and an assistant recommender carries verbatim review-span citation pointers (review_id + character offsets) into a shared knowledge base of 2,400 Yelp points of interest (restaurants, attractions, hotels) across 8 U.S. cities and 34,208 reviews. 29.4% of dialogues contain explicit reject_and_refine turns that probe recovery. The release contains 8,001 train / 999 validation / 1,000 test dialogues (stratified by city x POI-type, seed 42), 47 persona archetypes, four difficulty tiers, and an open-set candidate pool (~50-100 POIs per dialogue) alongside the closed 8-POI protocol. Companion artifacts: 14 baseline implementations and a 25-metric evaluation toolkit.",
  "alternateName": [
    "Tourism Recommendation with Accountable Citation Evidence",
    "TRACE Benchmark"
  ],
