  "version": "1.0.0",
  "datePublished": "2026-05-02",
  "inLanguage": "en",
  "isAccessibleForFree": true,
  "usageInfo": "Synthetic content authored by us (dialogue structure, non-quote turn text, grounding annotations, quote_spans positional metadata, code) is released under CC BY 4.0. Verbatim Yelp review text is NOT redistributed: in released dialogue text it appears as [Q:N] placeholders backed by positional metadata (review ID + character offsets), and is hydrated locally from a user-obtained Yelp Open Dataset bundle under the Yelp Dataset User Agreement (non-commercial, non-sublicensable, revocable; https://www.yelp.com/dataset). Yelp-derived POI metadata (name, address, lat/lon, categories, stars, price) is included under the Yelp ToU 4.E academic-publication carve-out. business_id and review_id values appear as bare factual identifiers. See NOTICE.md for the full clause-by-clause split.",
  "citeAs": "@inproceedings{zhao2026trace,\n  title  = {TRACE: Tourism Recommendation with Accountable Citation Evidence},\n  author = {Zhao, Zixu},\n  year   = {2026},\n  url    = {https://huggingface.co/datasets/taoist/TRACE}\n}",
  "rai:hasSyntheticData": true,
  "prov:wasGeneratedBy": {
    "@type": "prov:Activity",
    "rdfs:label": "TRACE synthetic-dialogue generation pipeline",
    "description": "Five-stage pipeline orchestrated by DSPy and executed by gpt-5.4-mini: (1) scenario construction conditioned on a persona archetype, (2) candidate POI selection (8 POIs sampled by stratified rating/category from the Yelp Open Dataset), (3) multi-turn dialogue generation with tier-specific reject_and_refine turns and verbatim review-span citations, (4) automated quality validation (turn structure, action coverage, POI/review references, per-quote fuzzy match >= 0.80 partial ratio), and (5) difficulty annotation (Easy/Medium/Hard/Expert) and stratified train/validation/test split (seed 42).",
    "prov:used": [
      {
        "@type": "prov:Entity",
        "rdfs:label": "gpt-5.4-mini",
        "description": "Large language model used as both the dialogue generator and the structured-output engine via DSPy signatures. Single-LLM dependence is documented in the dataset's known limitations."
      },
      {
        "@type": "prov:Entity",
        "rdfs:label": "DSPy",
        "description": "Programmatic-prompting framework providing typed signatures for action transitions, citation pointers, and grounding annotations during generation.",
        "url": "https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy"
      },
      {
        "@type": "prov:Entity",
        "rdfs:label": "Yelp Open Dataset",
        "description": "Source of business metadata, review IDs, and review text (used only at generation time; review text is NOT redistributed in the released dataset).",
        "url": "https://www.yelp.com/dataset"
      }
    ],
    "prov:startedAtTime": "2026-04-23T00:00:00Z",
    "prov:endedAtTime": "2026-04-24T23:59:59Z"
  },
  "rai:dataCollection": "Synthetic dialogues were generated with DSPy and gpt-5.4-mini conditioned on (a) one of 47 persona archetypes, (b) 8 candidate POIs sampled from the Yelp Open Dataset by stratified rating/category, and (c) tier-specific dialogue scenario prompts. The five-stage pipeline is: scenario construction, candidate POI selection, dialogue generation, automated quality validation (turn structure, action coverage, POI/review references, per-quote fuzzy match >= 0.80 partial ratio), and difficulty annotation (Easy/Medium/Hard/Expert).",
  "rai:dataAnnotationProtocol": "Per-turn annotations (action label, referenced_poi_ids, referenced_review_ids, acceptable_alternative_poi_ids, citation pointers, discovered_review_ids) are produced jointly with dialogue generation by the LLM under structured DSPy signatures and validated by automated checks. A secondary ALCE-style human evaluation pilot used five trained annotators rating 90 items (30 dialogues x 3 baselines: TF-IDF, RAG-Citation, LLM Zero-Shot) for citation precision, informativeness, and naturalness; Krippendorff's alpha is 0.31-0.58 across labels. Twenty additional dialogues received blind-written expert-author recommendations (POI Jaccard = 0.437, n=215).",
  "rai:dataPreprocessingProtocol": "POIs were drawn from the Yelp Open Dataset business and review files (yelp_academic_dataset_business.json, yelp_academic_dataset_review.json), filtered to 8 U.S. cities x 3 POI types x 100 POIs (= 2,400 POIs) with up to 15 reviews per POI (>= 5 minimum). Verbatim review spans cited by the LLM during dialogue generation were detected via fuzzy substring matching (>= 0.90 partial ratio) against the source review and replaced with [Q:N] placeholders. Quote-span metadata stores only (review_id, [start, end]) for exact quotes (~86% of cases) and (review_id, [start, end], edits) for near-verbatim quotes (~11%) where edits use whitelisted punctuation only (no Yelp word content). Splits are stratified by (city, difficulty) with seed 42.",
  "rai:dataReleaseMaintenancePlan": "The dataset is hosted on Hugging Face at https://huggingface.co/datasets/taoist/TRACE under CC BY 4.0 for our authored content. Versions follow semver (current: 1.0.0). Issues, bug reports, and dataset corrections are tracked via the HF dataset Discussions page. Maintenance commitment: active corrections for at least 24 months post-publication, with deprecated versions kept available via git revisions. Yelp-content reconstruction is guaranteed against any Yelp Open Dataset snapshot listed in the README compatibility matrix; new snapshots will be tested and added as Yelp publishes them.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": "Intended uses: (1) benchmarking conversational recommender systems on the joint axes of accuracy, citation grounding, and recovery; (2) studying the trade-off between LLM-style fluency and verbatim-evidence faithfulness in recommendation; (3) developing rejection-handling and aspect-synthesis techniques for multi-turn dialogue; (4) calibrating automated grounding metrics (CGS, NLI-entailment) against human judgments. Out-of-scope uses: production deployment for tourism advice without independent verification of POI accuracy, freshness, and licensing; commercial use of any Yelp-derived component without separate authorization from Yelp.",
  "rai:dataBiases": "Known biases: (1) Geographic - 8 mid-sized U.S. cities only (Indianapolis, Nashville, New Orleans, Philadelphia, Reno, Saint Louis, Tampa, Tucson); not representative of major metros, rural areas, or non-U.S. tourism. (2) Linguistic - U.S. English only; review style and user-preference expression follow Yelp/U.S. conventions. (3) Source - Yelp reviews skew toward businesses with strong online presence and active reviewer communities; long-tail or recently-opened venues are under-represented. (4) Persona - 47 hand-curated personas tilt toward common traveler archetypes; less coverage for accessibility-focused, elderly, or non-leisure travelers. (5) Generator - all dialogues come from a single LLM family (gpt-5.4-mini); stylistic patterns and reasoning biases of that model are inherited. (6) Visibility amplification - selecting top-rated POIs as candidates may reinforce attention to already popular venues.",
  "rai:dataLimitations": "Synthetic-dialogue artifact: dialogues are LLM-generated, not transcripts of real users, and may not capture full pragmatic complexity (multi-constraint negotiation, temporal availability, accessibility needs). Single-generator dependence: model-family-sensitive findings (notably rejection recovery) need cross-model replication. Open-set heterogeneity: baselines expose different candidate-access mechanisms; open-set comparisons are system-level rather than pure model quality. Human-eval scale: 90 items with five annotators is a calibration pilot, not a leaderboard. Grounding metric: composite CGS uses a hand-tuned CD/0.05 gate; baseline rankings should be cross-checked under alternative gates. Yelp dependency: the full knowledge base requires user-side reconstruction from a Yelp Open Dataset bundle; review text is not redistributed.",
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "Positive: pushes CRS evaluation toward verifiable, audited recommendations rather than opaque scoring, which is particularly important in high-stakes consumer decisions like travel and hospitality. Risks: (1) over-optimization toward citation-density proxies may encourage excessive verbatim quoting rather than semantically supported reasoning; (2) deployments on Yelp-style data may concentrate attention on already popular venues, contributing to overtourism and neighborhood-level visibility inequities; (3) Yelp reviews encode social, geographic, and demographic biases that propagate to systems trained or evaluated on TRACE; (4) tourism recommendation can be misused to surface or hide specific businesses for commercial gain. Users deploying TRACE-trained systems should audit recommendation distributions for fairness across neighborhoods, price tiers, and minority-owned businesses.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "The dataset does not contain personal data of real individuals. User personas are synthetic archetypes (e.g., 'budget-conscious solo traveler') and do not correspond to any real user. Yelp reviewer identifiers, user names, and account data are NOT included. POI references identify businesses (Yelp business_id) and review IDs (Yelp review_id) as bare factual identifiers; no reviewer-attributable text is redistributed. Content moderation: dialogues were generated under DSPy structured signatures with a system prompt that excludes personal-identifier fabrication; no manual safety review was performed beyond automated validation."
}